# An LTE rule whose MPM buffer is still incomplete at its hook is not a
# definitive no match: the engine is revisited in a later pass. Such a rule
# must not be dropped from the coverage counts by the no-match handling of that
# pass, otherwise a sibling evaluated later in the same walk applies the hook
# default policy while the rule is still pending.
#
# sid:100 carries the marker in the request line, which is split over packets 4
# and 6; at packet 4 the MPM is still in progress. sid:101 is the out of scope
# sibling at the same hook, last by sid. sid:101's no match must not apply the
# request_line default; sid:100 matches once the line completes (packet 6).
accept:hook http1:<response_complete $EXTERNAL_NET any -> $HOME_NET any (sid:9001;)

accept:flow,alert http1:<request_line $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET any (http.uri; content:"/index"; sid:100;)
accept:flow,alert http1:<request_line 198.51.100.0/24 any -> 198.51.100.0/24 any (sid:101;)
